config ZMK_NUMLOCK_LAYER_LED
    bool "NumLock LED follows numlock layer state instead of host HID indicator"
    default y
    help
      Drive the NumLock LED directly from the ZMK numlock layer's
      active/inactive state, rather than from the host-reported HID
      NumLock indicator. This keeps the LED in sync with the actual
      keyboard-side layer, and guarantees the LED is off after a
      power cycle (since the layer resets to the default layer).
